seg-ab053aadb65d = Earth and Moon point masses on a circular orbit, no Sun, no lunar gravity harmonics; the Earth's rotation axis is the orbit normal; the inertial frame equals the rotating frame at t = { "0" }; a spherical Moon; a synchronous lunar frame (no libration) except in <c1/>; the orbit is held known in the lunar axes in <c2/> (its error is carried by the orbiter range sigma); the orbiter family of <c3/> sees the line-of-sight integral of the k2 acceleration after a constant and a linear trend are removed, an upper-end figure.

